.Dd July 30, 2026
.Dt DISABLE-PANIC-DEBUGGER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm disable-panic-debugger
.Nd ensure auto-reboot-on-panic sysctls are configured
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
script ensures that
.Pa /etc/sysctl.conf
contains the following entries:
.Bd -literal
debug.debugger_on_panic=0
kern.panic_reboot_wait_time=5
kern.powercycle_on_panic=1
.Ed
.Pp
These cause the kernel to automatically
.Em power-cycle
after a panic rather than
dropping into the
.Xr ddb 4
debugger, and to wait five seconds before resetting so that console
messages are flushed.
A reboot without a power-cycle is not enough on a wedged box: firmware
must re-init devices.
This combination makes the host recoverable over
.Xr ssh 1
after a panic, without requiring physical console access.
A hang that never panics is
.Em not
covered; pair this with
.Pa enable-fail-watchdog.sh
and
.Pa activate_oneshot_be.sh
so
.Va bootfs
stays on the known-good boot environment.
.Pp
This is required on nested-virtualization development and test hosts
because a bug in the new nested-virt code path can panic the kernel
during
.Xr kldload 8
of
.Dq vmm
or during early register-virtualization tests.
Without auto-reboot, the operator would have to use a physical console
or IPMI to recover the host.
.Pp
The script is idempotent: running it repeatedly is safe and will append
each required line only once.
A line that is already present
.Pq either active or commented out
is reported as
.Em UNCHANGED .
A line that is appended is reported as
.Em SET .
The script always exits 0.
.Pp
After appending, the script queries the live values of both sysctls
via
.Xr sysctl 8
and prints them for operator visibility.
Note that the values written to
.Pa /etc/sysctl.conf
only take effect on the next reboot; the live values reflect the
current kernel state.
.Sh WARNING
This script is intended for development and test hosts only.
Disabling the kernel debugger on production systems removes a critical
fault-diagnosis tool.
Do
.Em not
install this script on production machines.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/etc/sysctl.conf"
.It Pa /etc/sysctl.conf
System-wide sysctl settings; the script appends to this file.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
script always exits 0.
It reports
.Em SET
when a line was appended and
.Em UNCHANGED
when the line was already present.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr loader.conf 5 ,
.Xr sysctl.conf 5 ,
.Xr kldload 8 ,
.Xr kldstat 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
script first appeared in the nested-virt register-virtualization
project in
.Fx 16.0 .
